# DWT templates

Which layout a page extends depends on what it is:

| Page | Extends |
| --- | --- |
| In-service page, v2–v4 | `layouts/vN.html` (its own version) |
| In-service page, v1 | `layouts/main.html` |
| Prototype index, `versions/vN.html`, `about-this-service.html` | `layouts/prototype-hub.html` |

`layouts/vN.html` extends `prototype-hub.html`, which extends `main.html`, which extends `govuk-prototype-kit/layouts/govuk-branded.njk`.

Every in-service page starts with:

```nunjucks
{% extends "layouts/v4.html" %}

{% set version = "v4" %}
{% set pageName = "Software providers" %}
{% set activeSection = "providers" %}
```

- `version` builds the navigation and every link (`href="/{{ version }}/software-providers"`). Never hard-code `/v4/` in a page.
- `activeSection` is `"home"`, `"providers"` or `"regulators"` in v3 and v4 (the layout also reads `"organisations"`, set by the v1 and v2 placeholder route). It highlights the navigation item.
- The prototype phase banner is only on hub pages (index, about this service), in `beforeContent`:
  ```nunjucks
  {{ govukPhaseBanner({ tag: { text: "Prototype" }, html: 'This is a prototype. It is not a real service.' }) }}
  ```
  Don't add it to in-service pages.
- Back links: sub-pages use `govukBackLink` in `beforeContent` with a real `href` built from `version` (e.g. back to the provider detail page), not `javascript:history.back()`. Top-level pages (start, section lists) have none.
- Start pages show a heading, one line of text and a bulleted list of links. They don't use the green "Start now" button.
- Forms: `method="post"`, `novalidate`, action built from `version`. Error summary at the top of the content block, as in `v4/software-providers/add.html`.
- Page titles: `pageName` is the page title, and the layout adds " - DWT admin portal". A question page uses the question as its title. An error page starts with "Error: " (WCAG 2.4.2). v5 titles: the name page is "What is the name of the software provider and package?", the Manage page is "Manage client credentials".
- Use a `govuk-caption-l` above the `h1` to name the section on sub-pages (e.g. "Software providers").
- Repeated content goes in a partial with a leading underscore, included by version (`{% include version + "/software-providers/_email-addresses.html" %}`).
- Pages are `.html`. The "related items" sidebar from the common templates isn't used in this prototype — don't introduce it without asking.
